# Fitbit Data Analysis & Machine Learning Midterm Project

## Overview

This project focuses on analyzing Fitbit-inspired health and activity data using machine learning and data analytics techniques. The goal was to explore how wearable fitness data can be processed, visualized, and used to identify meaningful behavioral and wellness patterns.

The project combines data preprocessing, exploratory data analysis, visualization, and predictive modeling techniques to better understand relationships between physical activity, calories burned, and overall fitness trends.

Dataset Information

This project uses Fitbit-inspired fitness tracking data for machine learning and health analytics.

Dataset Features:
- Step count
- Calories burned
- Activity intensity
- Sleep data
- Daily wellness metrics

Preprocessing Steps:
- Data cleaning
- Missing value handling
- Duplicate removal
- Feature engineering
- Normalization

The dataset supports exploratory analysis and machine learning prediction workflows.
